"Each day with recorded training sets counts once, even if you complete several workouts. This week's count follows your calendar settings and is compared with your current weekly target." = "Each day with recorded training sets counts once, even if you complete several workouts. This week's count follows your calendar settings and is compared with your current weekly target.";

"Only logged workout days count toward your weekly target. The two recovery shades are a simple display rule, not a measurement of muscle recovery or workout intensity." = "Only logged workout days count toward your weekly target. The two recovery shades are a simple display rule, not a measurement of muscle recovery or workout intensity.";

"Why this target?" = "Why this target?";

"Your fixed gram targets use the weight, training goal and weekly training frequency saved in Masso. If you are 65 or older, the protein factor is raised modestly. Meal count only divides the daily targets; it does not change them." = "Your fixed gram targets use the weight, training goal and weekly training frequency saved in Masso. If you are 65 or older, the protein factor is raised modestly. Meal count only divides the daily targets; it does not change them.";

"Carbohydrate uses your goal and planned training days, with a 130 g adult reference floor. Fat uses a simple 0.8 g/kg planning value. These are practical estimates, not measured calorie needs or medical prescriptions." = "Carbohydrate uses your goal and planned training days, with a 130 g adult reference floor. Fat uses a simple 0.8 g/kg planning value. These are practical estimates, not measured calorie needs or medical prescriptions.";

"Masso does not currently collect height or body composition, so it cannot estimate energy needs precisely. Sleep duration is not used to change macro grams because there is no established formula for doing that." = "Masso does not currently collect height or body composition, so it cannot estimate energy needs precisely. Sleep duration is not used to change macro grams because there is no established formula for doing that.";

"ISSN describes protein needs as a range, not one proven ideal for every person. Masso selects a fixed planning point from body weight and training goal; carbohydrates also reflect planned weekly training days, and fat uses a simple weight-based estimate. Age modestly raises the protein factor from 65 onward. Height, body composition, medical conditions and reliable daily energy expenditure are not collected, so these values are estimates rather than a personalized clinical prescription. Sleep data is not used to change macro targets because there is no established conversion from sleep duration to daily macro grams. Scoring weights and color bands are product choices, not research-validated health scores." = "ISSN describes protein needs as a range, not one proven ideal for every person. Masso selects a fixed planning point from body weight and training goal; carbohydrates also reflect planned weekly training days, and fat uses a simple weight-based estimate. Age modestly raises the protein factor from 65 onward. Height, body composition, medical conditions and reliable daily energy expenditure are not collected, so these values are estimates rather than a personalized clinical prescription. Sleep data is not used to change macro targets because there is no established conversion from sleep duration to daily macro grams. Scoring weights and color bands are product choices, not research-validated health scores.";

